invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: ct.h takes a native copy outside a host object, so a build that
  states nothing about the multiply can carry the native multiply under
  the _native names, where lint-trust-separation lists files and not what
  they compile to. test/widemul-builds.sh requires
  -DCH_WIDEMUL_NATIVE_COPY alone not to compile.

--- old
#if defined(CH_WIDEMUL_NATIVE_COPY) && !defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME)
#error "a _native copy (widemul_native.h) compiles into a host object alone"
#endif
--- new
